  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Search Parameters**\n\nI\'m currently focused on extracting and understanding user search parameters. I\'ve successfully isolated the search query, wilaya, commune, and category from the input elements. Lowercasing the search query seems a good approach for consistency. The next step involves figuring out how to use these distinct pieces of information to filter the data.\n\n\n**Refining Geographic Filtering**\n\nI\'m now refining the geographic filtering logic. The current code assumes a simple \"place, state\" format from the `wilaya` field, parsing it with a simple split. I realize this might not handle multi-part place names well (e.g., \"Something, Bab Ezzouar, Alger\"). I\'m considering edge cases. It\'s becoming clearer that the format from Nominatim is designed to avoid this case. Now I need to consider cases where Nominatim is not involved.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
