  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Code Implementation**\n\nI\'ve decided to leverage `grep` to streamline modifications across `src/app.js` and `src/admin.js`, also removing `src/firebase.js`. Further, I\'m now honing in on `supabase-init.sql`, particularly the Supabase import and usage context, before fully implementing `src/supabase.js`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Code Dependencies**\n\nOkay, I\'m taking a more focused approach now. I realize that manually editing large files like `src/app.js` with `edit_file` might be unwieldy. So, I\'m considering a smaller Node script or chunk-wise edits for the modifications needed. I\'m currently cross-referencing imports in `app.js` with their uses, like `signInAnonymously`, `GoogleAuthProvider`, and the various Firestore and Storage functions.\n\n\n**Simplifying Integration Approach**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing simplicity based on recent insights. Direct substitution of Firebase with Supabase across `app.js` and `admin.js` presents complexities due to API differences and significant manual edits. My plan is to leverage Supabase JS directly instead. This avoids a wrapper implementation and leverages the two files. The core focus will now be on how to use Supabase, focusing on `auth.signInAnonymously`, `auth.signInWithOAuth`, and `auth.onAuthStateChange`. I will use `ref`, `uploadBytes`, and `getDownloadURL` from Supabase.\n\n\n**Mapping Code Functionality**\n\nI\'m now methodically mapping the functionality in `src/app.js` to its Supabase equivalent. Focusing on authentication, I\'m noting the changes needed for `signInAnonymously`, `onAuthStateChanged`, and `signOut`. I\'m also preparing for how to handle Google sign-in with `signInWithOAuth`, which has the corresponding Supabase call. In parallel, I\'m working to adapt the \'Load Reports\' section to the Supabase equivalent using `.select(\'*\')` and `.order()`. I will rename `createdAt` and `photo_url` to match the data.\n\n\n**Implementing Realtime Updates**\n\nI\'m now integrating realtime functionality using Supabase channels. I\'m focusing on the `reports` table to listen for inserts and updates.  I\'m implementing a `subscribeRealtime()` function to monitor database changes. My focus is payload handling and mapping Firebase\'s `INSERT` and `UPDATE` events to Supabase equivalents.\n```javascript\nfunction subscribeRealtime() {\n  supabase.channel(\'public:reports\')\n    .on(\'postgres_changes\', { event: \'*\', schema: \'public\', table: \'reports\' }, payload => {\n      // payload.new, payload.old, payload.eventType\n      // \'INSERT\', \'UPDATE\'\n    })\n    .subscribe();\n}\n```\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'m translating Firebase functions to Supabase calls. For upvoting, I\'m switching from Firestore\'s `increment` to a Supabase RPC or, alternatively, an update. I\'ve updated the confirmations insert as well. Regarding status updates, the `updateDoc` call in Firebase is replaced with `supabase.from(\'reports\').update` with a specific ID filter. And lastly, I\'m adapting the image file upload logic to Supabase Storage, with the path using the file ID.\n```javascript\n// Supabase upvote (could use RPC)\nawait supabase.rpc(\'increment_votes\', { row_id: id });\nawait supabase.from(\'confirmations\').insert({ email, report_id: id });\n\n// Supabase\nawait supabase.from(\'reports\').update({ status: nextStatus }).eq(\'id\', id);\n\n// Supabase\nconst { data, error } = await supabase.storage.from(\'photos\').upload(id + \'.jpg\', photoFile)\n```\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 740080579
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
