  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Detailing Supabase Setup**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the environment variables are active within the application. I can now guide the user on the Supabase configuration. My next step is to tell them to navigate to the Supabase SQL editor and open `supabase_init.sql` using a specific URL. This will let them perform the setup steps easily.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Awesome. The app is completely migrated to use your new Supabase project credentials in the `.env` file!\n\nTo get your database actually running and to host it on Supabase, here are the final steps you need to take in your Supabase dashboard:\n\n### 1. Setup the Database and Storage\nI created a file for you named `supabase_init.sql` (you can find it in the file explorer on the left or top left).\n\n1. Go to your **Supabase Dashboard**: [SQL Editor for your project](https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/bjqhwgskffdccrmveuxg/sql/new)\n2. Open `supabase_init.sql` in this editor, copy **all** the content inside it.\n3. Paste the code into the Supabase SQL Editor and click the **Run** button at the bottom right.\n*(This will automatically create all your tables: `reports`, `confirmations`, `audit_log`, `admins`, `allowed_emails`, setup your Realtime connections, setup Row Level Security (RLS) policies, and create a `photos` storage bucket).*\n\n### 2. Enable Google Authentication\nSince the app uses Google Login for admins, you need to enable it in Supabase:\n\n1. Go to your **Authentication Providers**: [Auth Providers for your project](https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/bjqhwgskffdccrmveuxg/auth/providers)\n2. Click on **Google** and toggle \"Enable Google\".\n3. You will need a **Client ID** and **Client Secret**. You can get these by creating an OAuth client in the [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials).\n4. When configuring Google Cloud, it will ask for an \"Authorized redirect URI\". You must paste this exact link:\n`https://bjqhwgskffdccrmveuxg.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback`\n\n### 3. Setup Your Admin Account (Optional but recommended)\nRight now, the public UI works, but to use the Admin Dashboard, the `admins` table needs a user.\n\n1. Go to your app\'s admin login page (`/admin.html`)\n2. Use the \"Se connecter avec email\" block and try to sign up with `aymen` as the email, and `19981998` as the password. \nOr, login with Google. \n*(If you sign in, the database will log your account).*\n\nOnce the SQL has been run, your application should be 100% functional and hosted smoothly on modern Supabase! Let me know if you run into any permission or connection issues, and we\'ll squash them."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 490932262
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
