    }
  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying User Intent**\n\nI\'m now focused on understanding the user\'s intent: they need instructions for Google OAuth setup within Google Cloud, specifically for use with Supabase. I\'m prioritizing the Google Cloud configuration aspects, as that\'s where the user seems to be facing challenges, and I need to make the instructions relevant to their specific setup. I will prioritize the use of Supabase in relation to OAuth and Google Cloud.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "To set up Google OAuth for your Supabase project, you need to create OAuth credentials in the Google Cloud Console and then add them to your Supabase project. \n\nHere is the step-by-step guide:\n\n### Part 1: Configure Google Cloud\n1. Go to the [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/) and sign in.\n2. Select an existing project from the dropdown at the top, or create a **New Project**.\n3. In the left sidebar, navigate to **APIs & Services** > **OAuth consent screen**.\n   * Choose **External** (if you want any Google user to be able to sign in) and click **Create**.\n   * Fill in the required fields (App name, User support email, Developer contact email). You can skip the rest for now. Click **Save and Continue** through the next steps.\n   * *Note: While testing, your app will be in \"Testing\" mode, so you might need to add your own email to the \"Test users\" list on the consent screen if you want to be able to log in.*\n4. Now, go to **Credentials** in the left sidebar.\n5. Click **+ CREATE CREDENTIALS** at the top and select **OAuth client ID**.\n6. Select **Web application** as the Application type. Give it a name (e.g., \"Supabase Auth\").\n7. Under **Authorized JavaScript origins**, click **ADD URI** and enter your Supabase project URL:\n   `https://bjqhwgskffdccrmveuxg.supabase.co`\n8. Under **Authorized redirect URIs**, click **ADD URI** and enter your Supabase callback URL:\n   `https://bjqhwgskffdccrmveuxg.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback`\n9. Click **Create**.\n10. A popup will appear with your **Client ID** and **Client Secret**. Copy both of these; you will need them for Supabase.\n\n### Part 2: Connect it to Supabase\n1. Go to your [Supabase Dashboard](https://supabase.com/dashboard) and open your project.\n2. In the left sidebar, go to **Authentication** > **Providers**.\n3. Find **Google** in the list and click to open it.\n4. Toggle **Enable Sign in with Google** to the ON position.\n5. Paste the **Client ID** and **Client Secret** you got from Google into the respective fields.\n6. Click **Save**.\n\nThat\'s it! Your application is now configured to allow users to sign in using their Google accounts via Supabase. Make sure you\'ve also run the `supabase_init.sql` script in your Supabase SQL Editor so all your tables and security policies are set up correctly."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 235219823
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
