  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating the Analysis**\n\nI\'ve begun dissecting the user\'s input. It\'s a snapshot of the Google Auth Platform overview page within the GCP console. The key issue? It indicates the platform isn\'t configured, urging the user to \"Get started.\" This is the core of the matter to be addressed.\n\n\n**Defining the OAuth Flow**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specific steps for the user\'s Google OAuth setup within Google Cloud, to integrate with their Supabase project. The user\'s goal seems to be to configure Google Auth in GCP for use with Supabase. I\'ve broken it down into actionable steps: Clicking \"Get Started,\" configuring the consent screen (branding), and then creating an OAuth Client ID for a web application. The essential part is setting the correct Redirect URI for the Supabase project: `https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback`.\n\n\n**Outlining the Procedure**\n\nI\'ve refined the procedural steps for the user. I have finalized detailed instructions, including emphasizing the \"External\" audience type and branding information. I\'ve also clarified the client creation process within the Google Cloud Console. Now, I\'m integrating these steps into the response, ensuring conciseness and clarity for easy implementation.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Perfect, you are in exactly the right place! Since you are using Supabase for your backend, you need to create the Google OAuth credentials here and then paste them into your Supabase dashboard. \n\nHere is exactly what you need to do step-by-step:\n\n### Step 1: Configure the Consent Screen\n1. Click that blue **Get started** button in your screenshot.\n2. Select **External** (so anyone with a Google account can sign in) and click Create.\n3. Fill in the **App Information** (App name: \"Hafra DZ\", and select your email for support/developer contact).\n4. You can skip through the \"Scopes\" and \"Test users\" sections for now by just clicking **Save and Continue**.\n\n### Step 2: Create the OAuth Client\n1. On the left menu, click on **Clients** (or \"Credentials\" if it redirects you there).\n2. Click **Create Client** (or \"Create Credentials\" -> \"OAuth client ID\" at the top).\n3. Select **Web application** as the Application type. Name it something like \"Supabase Auth\".\n\n### Step 3: Add your Supabase Redirect URI (Crucial!)\n1. Scroll down to **Authorized redirect URIs**.\n2. Click **Add URI**.\n3. Based on your project code, paste this exact Supabase callback URL:\n   `https://bjqhwgskffdccrmveuxg.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback`\n4. Click **Create**.\n\n### Step 4: Link to Supabase\n1. Google will now show you a popup with your **Client ID** and **Client Secret**. Copy both of these.\n2. Go to your **Supabase Dashboard**.\n3. Navigate to **Authentication** -> **Providers** -> **Google**.\n4. Turn on the \"Enable Google\" switch.\n5. Paste your **Client ID** and **Client Secret** into the respective fields.\n6. Click **Save**.\n\nOnce you do this, your `supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth({ provider: \'google\' })` code will successfully open the Google login screen and redirect back to your app!"
