    modified_response: "To set up Google OAuth for your Supabase project, you need to connect the two platforms. Here is the step-by-step guide based on where you are right now.\n\n### Step 1: Configure Google Cloud (First Screenshot)\n1. On that page, click the blue **Get started** button.\n2. It will ask you to configure your **OAuth Consent Screen**. \n   - Choose **External** (unless you have a Google Workspace and only want internal users).\n   - Fill in the required fields like App Name, User support email, and Developer contact information. You can skip the logo and domains for now.\n   - Click \"Save and Continue\" through the Scopes and Test Users screens.\n3. Once the consent screen is set up, go to **Clients** (or \"Credentials\" in the older menu on the left).\n4. Click **Create Client** (or \"Create Credentials\" > \"OAuth client ID\").\n5. Application type: Select **Web application**.\n6. Name: Give it a name like \"Supabase Auth\".\n7. **Authorized JavaScript origins**: Put your Supabase project URL. Based on your code, it should be:\n   ```text\n   https://bjqhwgskffdccrmveuxg.supabase.co\n   ```\n8. **Authorized redirect URIs**: Put exactly this URL (your Supabase URL + `/auth/v1/callback`):\n   ```text\n   https://bjqhwgskffdccrmveuxg.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback\n   ```\n9. Click **Create**.\n10. A modal will appear with your **Client ID** and **Client Secret**. Keep this window open or copy those two values.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Configure Supabase (Second Screenshot)\n1. On the left menu in Supabase, under **CONFIGURATION**, click **Sign In / Providers**.\n2. Scroll down until you find **Google** and click to open its settings.\n3. Toggle \"Enable Sign in with Google\" to **ON**.\n4. Paste the **Client ID** you got from Google Cloud.\n5. Paste the **Client Secret** you got from Google Cloud.\n6. Click **Save**.\n\nThat\'s it! Your Google login (`supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth({ provider: \'google\' })`) should now redirect securely through Google and register users into your Supabase project. They will appear in the \"Users\" list shown in your second screenshot once they log in for the first time."
