  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing OAuth Configuration**\n\nI\'m currently focused on configuring Google OAuth within Supabase and Google Cloud, specifically regarding the setup outlined in the provided screenshots. I\'m looking at the Google Cloud OAuth overview, the Supabase Auth Users tab, and the Google Cloud OAuth Client ID configuration details, particularly the Authorized JavaScript origins and redirect URIs. I\'m seeking to understand how these elements interrelate for a successful integration.\n\n\n**Clarifying OAuth Steps**\n\nI\'ve clarified the steps for setting up Google Auth with Supabase, detailing the Google Cloud Console and Supabase Dashboard configurations. Key configurations involve the OAuth consent screen and creating OAuth client IDs (Web application). Specifically, I\'ve outlined setting Authorized redirect URIs in Google Cloud to `https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback` and the importance of pasting the Client ID and Secret in Supabase. I have not included any steps for configuring JavaScript origins, assuming no frontend component for now.\n\n\n**Refining OAuth Integration**\n\nI\'m now refining the OAuth integration steps, recognizing the specific challenges of embedded environments like AI Studio. I\'ve re-examined the third screenshot and confirmed the correct Supabase backend configuration using `https://bjqhwgskffdccrmveuxg.supabase.co` as the authorized JavaScript origin and redirect URI. I\'ve added a crucial step to address the user\'s redirect concern: the app\'s URL should be added in Supabase\'s URL Configuration under Authentication to ensure proper redirection after user authentication, especially relevant for embedded environments like AI Studio.\n\n\n**Implementing OAuth Integration**\n\nI\'m now fully implementing Google OAuth integration. I\'ve documented the exact steps: enabling Google in Supabase, copying the Client ID and Secret from Google Cloud, and pasting them into Supabase. I\'ve also detailed setting the App Redirect URL in Supabase under URL Configuration. Finally, I\'ve noted a crucial step, and a specific issue to consider when testing in environments like AI Studio (iframe blocking) and the need to open the app in a new tab.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Based on your screenshots, you have successfully created the Google Cloud OAuth client and correctly set the Supabase callback route! You are almost there. \n\nHere are the final steps to connect them:\n\n### 1. Enable Google Provider in Supabase\n1. In your **Supabase Dashboard** (from your last screenshot), look at the left sidebar under the **CONFIGURATION** section.\n2. Click on **Sign In / Providers**.\n3. Find **Google** in the list and click on it to expand it.\n4. Toggle **Enable Sign in with Google** to turn it on.\n5. Go back to your **Google Cloud Console** (your 3rd screenshot) and copy the **Client ID** and **Client secret** (from the right-hand panel).\n6. Paste them into the corresponding fields in the Supabase Google provider settings.\n7. Click **Save**.\n\n### 2. Configure \331\220App Redirect URLs in Supabase\nSupabase needs to know where to send the user back after they successfully log in.\n1. In the Supabase left sidebar, click on **URL Configuration**.\n2. Under **Site URL**, paste your application\'s base URL. Since you are in AI Studio, you should use your Shared App URL: `https://ais-pre-tzrv7lccl66m3m6zdmmk6n-558616716698.europe-west2.run.app`\n3. Under **Redirect URLs**, click **Add URL** and add your Development App URL as well so it works while you are coding: `https://ais-dev-tzrv7lccl66m3m6zdmmk6n-558616716698.europe-west2.run.app`\n\n### \360\237\232\250 Critical Note for Testing Logging In \360\237\232\250\nGoogle **does not allow** its login screen to be displayed inside an iframe (which is how the AI Studio preview window works). \n\nIf you try to click \"Sign in with Google\" inside the AI Studio preview window, it will block it and show an error. \n**To test the login, you MUST open your app in a new tab.** You can do this by clicking the \"Open app in new tab\" icon at the top right of the preview window."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 913168967
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
