    thinking: "**Analyzing Authentication Systems**\n\nI\'m currently examining the user\'s setup, a mix of Google Analytics, Firebase, and Supabase. Their primary hurdle seems to be integrating Google OAuth with Supabase. I\'ve reviewed screenshots of their Google Cloud Console (OAuth Overview and Client ID sections) and their Supabase Authentication Users section, which are currently empty. The next step is to understand if they have configured API keys, and secret keys correctly.\n\n\n**Reviewing OAuth Configuration**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the user created a web application OAuth client ID in Google Cloud Console, noting the client ID and secret. The authorized origins and redirect URIs seem correctly configured. I\'m now focusing on the Supabase setup. I\'ll guide the user on enabling the Google provider within Supabase, and carefully inputting the client ID and secret. Then, I will confirm the configuration of  `supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth({ provider: \'google\' })`.\n\n\n**Clarifying Redirect Behavior**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of redirect URLs and OAuth flows within Supabase. I\'ve realized the user needs guidance on handling redirects in their client code. Supabase defaults to the Site URL if no redirect is specified, but we can override this using `redirectTo` with `signInWithOAuth`. Specifically for AI Studio apps, which need to be tested outside of the iframe, `window.location.origin` may not always be accurate, so a precise URL is best. I will guide them to check the dashboard.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "It looks like you have correctly created the OAuth credentials in Google Cloud! The next step is to take those credentials and plug them into your **Supabase** dashboard so Supabase knows how to talk to Google.\n\nHere is exactly what you need to do next in **Supabase**:\n\n### 1. Enable Google Provider in Supabase\nIn your Supabase Dashboard (like in your screenshots):\n1. On the left menu under **Configuration**, click **Sign In / Providers** (often just labeled **Providers**).\n2. Find **Google** in the list of providers and click it to expand.\n3. Toggle the switch to **Enable Sign in with Google**.\n4. Copy the **Client ID** from your Google Cloud Console screenshot (`474894363749...apps.googleusercontent.com`) and paste it into the \"Client ID\" field.\n5. Copy the **Client Secret** from your Google Cloud Console and paste it into the \"Client Secret\" field.\n6. Click **Save**.\n\n### 2. Configure Site URL and Redirects\nSupabase needs to know where to send the user back to after they log in with Google.\n1. On the left menu under **Configuration**, click **URL Configuration**.\n2. Set the **Site URL** to your app\'s URL. For AI Studio, you can put:\n   `https://ais-pre-tzrv7lccl66m3m6zdmmk6n-558616716698.europe-west2.run.app`\n3. Just below that, under **Redirect URLs**, click \"Add URL\" and add your development URL as well so it works when you are editing:\n   `https://ais-dev-tzrv7lccl66m3m6zdmmk6n-558616716698.europe-west2.run.app`\n\n### 3. Let\'s make sure the code redirects to the right place\nI\'ll quickly update the sign-in code in your app to ensure it redirects back precisely to the page you are on.\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 780172234
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
