  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying Domain Authorization**\n\nI am now focusing on providing actionable steps for authorized domain setup. I\'m prioritizing Google Cloud Console and Supabase, as the hosting environment heavily influences the instructions. I want to clearly explain *why* domain authorization is critical, tying it directly to the user\'s application deployment location.\n\n\n**Addressing Vercel Integration**\n\nNow I\'m making sure domain configuration for Vercel is crystal clear. I\342\200\231ve refined the steps, specifically differentiating the setup within Google Cloud Console and Supabase, now considering that Vercel hosting means Google Cloud doesn\'t require Vercel\'s URL directly, as Supabase manages the OAuth flow. I\'m focusing on the *essential* Supabase URL configurations: Site URL and Redirect URLs.\n\n\n**Refining Supabase Configuration**\n\nNow I\'m completely clarifying the Supabase OAuth flow and how it relates to Google Cloud Console. I realized the user\'s Google Cloud configuration is likely already correct, focusing the user on their Supabase settings. Specifically, I\'m identifying where to input the application URLs for both the Site URL and Redirect URLs within Supabase\'s authentication settings. I\'m also reminding them to enable Google as a provider within Supabase.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "If you plan to host the app on **Vercel**, here is exactly how to connect everything. The good news is that your Google Cloud Console is already correctly configured to talk to Supabase! You just need to finish the setup inside Supabase.\n\nHere are the 2 things you need to do in the Supabase Dashboard:\n\n### Step 1: Enable Google in Supabase\nRight now, Supabase doesn\'t know your Google credentials.\n1. In your Supabase Dashboard, look at the left sidebar (under **Configuration**) and click on **Sign In / Providers**.\n2. Scroll through the list and click on **Google**.\n3. Toggle the switch to **Enable Sign in with Google**.\n4. Go back to your Google Cloud Console tab, copy the **Client ID** and **Client secret**.\n5. Paste them into the corresponding fields in Supabase.\n6. Click **Save**.\n\n### Step 2: Tell Supabase about your Vercel App\nWhen a user logs in, Supabase needs to know where to send them back to. By default, it uses `localhost:3000`. You need to add your Vercel URL.\n1. Deploy your app to Vercel to get your live URL (e.g., `https://hafra-dz.vercel.app`).\n2. In the Supabase sidebar (under **Configuration**), click on **URL Configuration**.\n3. Under **Site URL**, paste your Vercel app\'s URL.\n4. Under **Redirect URLs**, click **Add URL** and add your Vercel URL with `/*` at the end (e.g., `https://hafra-dz.vercel.app/*`). This tells Supabase it\'s safe to redirect users anywhere on your site.\n\n**Want to test it here in AI Studio first?**\nAdd these URLs to your Supabase **Redirect URLs** so it works right here in the preview window:\n- `https://ais-dev-tzrv7lccl66m3m6zdmmk6n-558616716698.europe-west2.run.app/*`\n- `https://ais-pre-tzrv7lccl66m3m6zdmmk6n-558616716698.europe-west2.run.app/*`\n\nOnce you\'ve done Step 1, the Google login should start functioning!"
    thinking_duration {
