  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Independence**\n\nI\'m exploring the implications of removing dependencies on the AI Studio platform. The core aim is to achieve an independent codebase, enabling deployment without ties to specific branding or infrastructure. The goal is to maximize portability and control, but I need to understand the development tradeoffs.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "To host your app completely independently without any ties to Google AI Studio, you can export your code and host it on a platform like Vercel, Netlify, or GitHub Pages. Your app is a standard web application (HTML/JS/CSS with Vite) and uses standard Supabase, so it\'s fully portable!\n\nHere is how you can do it:\n\n### Step 1: Export your code from AI Studio\n1. Look at the code editor panel on the right side of the screen.\n2. In the top-right corner of the editor, click the **Export** button (it usually looks like an arrow pointing down or a download icon, or you can find it in the project settings menu).\n3. Choose **Download ZIP** (or Export to GitHub if you prefer).\n4. If you downloaded a ZIP, extract it on your computer.\n\n### Step 2: Deploy to Vercel (Easiest Method)\nSince you mentioned Vercel earlier, here is the easiest way to host it there:\n\n1. Create a free account on [GitHub](https://github.com/) and [Vercel](https://vercel.com/) if you don\'t have them.\n2. Upload your extracted folder to a new repository on GitHub.\n3. Go to your Vercel Dashboard and click **Add New Project**.\n4. Import your newly created GitHub repository.\n5. In the Vercel deployment settings, make sure to add your Environment Variables. Expand the **Environment Variables** section and add:\n   - `VITE_SUPABASE_URL`: `your_supabase_url`\n   - `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`: `your_supabase_anon_key`\n6. Click **Deploy**. Vercel will build your app and give you a live URL (like `your-app.vercel.app`).\n\n### Step 3: Update Supabase OAuth Settings\nOnce you have your new Vercel URL (or any other domain you use), you **must** tell Supabase and Google Cloud to trust it:\n\n1. **In Google Cloud Console:**\n   - Go to APIs & Services > Credentials > OAuth 2.0 Client IDs.\n   - Add your new Vercel URL (e.g., `https://your-app.vercel.app`) to the **Authorized JavaScript origins**.\n\n2. **In Supabase:**\n   - Go to Authentication > URL Configuration.\n   - Update the **Site URL** to your new Vercel URL.\n   - You don\'t need to change `Authorized redirect URIs` or the `Redirect URIs` in Google Cloud as they still point to your Supabase project domain, which acts as the middleman!\n\nThat\'s it! Once deployed on Vercel, your app will be completely independent of AI Studio."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 717065349
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
