    modified_response: "You will need to use your actual Supabase URL and Anon Key when you deploy to Vercel. \n\nHere is exactly how it works:\n\n1. **In your code**: In `src/supabase.js`, we have code that looks for the environment variables (`VITE_SUPABASE_URL` and `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`). If it doesn\'t find them, it uses the hardcoded ones we put in earlier.\n2. **On Vercel**: You shouldn\'t leave the keys hardcoded in your `src/supabase.js` file if you make your code public on GitHub. Instead, you should provide them securely to Vercel.\n\n**Steps to set them in Vercel:**\n1. Go to your Vercel Project Dashboard.\n2. Go to **Settings** > **Environment Variables**.\n3. Add a new variable:\n   - **Key**: `VITE_SUPABASE_URL`\n   - **Value**: `https://bjqhwgskffdccrmveuxg.supabase.co`  *(your actual Supabase URL)*\n4. Add another variable:\n   - **Key**: `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`\n   - **Value**: *(Your long anon key starting with `eyJhb...`)*\n5. Click **Save** for both.\n6. Trigger a new deployment in Vercel so it builds the app with these new variables.\n\nBy doing this, Vercel will automatically inject your Supabase credentials into the app when it builds it, and your app will securely connect to your Supabase project without needing \"Google AI Studio\" in the middle!"
