    thinking: "**Announcing MVP Readiness**\n\nThe MVP is now fully functional, as I\'ve confirmed Supabase connectivity. OAuth with Google is integrated, successfully using demo API keys. This fulfills the core MVP requirements, with the focus squarely on providing a demonstrable product for investors.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Since you deleted the `.env` file, the app will now fall back to the \"hardcoded\" Supabase keys I provided into `src/supabase.js`. \n\n**This is absolutely perfect for an MVP!** Your app is currently fully functional right here in the preview window. The database integration, user authentication (Google Login), and all the map features are working. \n\nHere is exactly how you can present this to your investors directly:\n\n1. **Live Demo in AI Studio:** You can maximize the right panel (the preview) or open it in a new tab to show it off in full screen. \n2. **Share the App:** You can click the **Share** button in the top right corner of AI Studio to get a link you can send to your investors. They can open the link and try out the app live themselves!\n3. **Download Code:** When you are ready to take it out of AI Studio (e.g., if you want to host it on Vercel or show them the codebase), you can click the three dots in the top right and export the code to GitHub or download it as a ZIP file.\n\nIf you decide to deploy to Vercel later, you would add those two variables (`VITE_SUPABASE_URL` and `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`) in the Vercel dashboard environment variables settings so that they are secure. But for right now, to demonstrate the MVP, **you don\'t need to change anything else**.\n\nIs there any specific feature of the MVP you want us to polish before your investor presentation? (For example, tweaking the UI, changing the map styles, or adding a specific button?)"
