  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Deployment Options**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the user\'s explicit desire to deploy to Vercel. Their previous interest in Supabase and the MVP context is informing my approach. I\'m prioritizing simplicity, efficiency, and a solution focused on getting the app, minus Google AI, live as quickly as possible, ideally for investor showcasing.\n\n\n**Outlining Deployment Strategy**\n\nI\'m now outlining the steps to deploy to Vercel. I\'ve broken it down into exporting from AI Studio (likely to GitHub), then importing to Vercel. I will detail how the user needs to set environment variables in Vercel to connect to Supabase (URL and Anon Key). Finally, I will note the need to ensure redirect URIs are updated in Supabase and Google Cloud Console to match the new deployment URL.\n\n\n**Clarifying Deployment Steps**\n\nI\'m checking the codebase to ensure Vite\'s handling of routing, so a `vercel.json` file may be unnecessary. The build process, with `npm run build` outputting to `dist`, is straightforward for Vercel. I plan to give step-by-step instructions. These include exporting from AI Studio to GitHub, importing to Vercel, and configuring Supabase environment variables.\n\n\n**Confirming Vercel Deployment**\n\nI\'ve outlined crucial environment variable steps for Supabase integration within Vercel\'s deployment process. These variables, `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` and `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, are critical for establishing the Supabase connection. I\'ve also emphasized the vital need to update OAuth redirects within both Supabase and the Google Cloud Console to ensure authorization flows correctly. I\'m now checking the app for routing, and am considering adding a `vercel.json` if necessary for SPA routing.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Deploying a Vite application to Vercel is the perfect choice for an MVP. Since we have our backend on Supabase, Vercel will only host the frontend, which makes it fast and completely removes the \"Google AI Studio\" environment from your final link.\n\nHere is the step-by-step guide to deploying your app to Vercel:\n\n### 1. Export your Code from AI Studio\n1. Click the **Menu / Settings** icon in the top left or top right of Google AI Studio.\n2. Choose **Export to GitHub** (or \"Download ZIP\" and upload it to a GitHub repository manually).\n\n### 2. Import into Vercel\n1. Create an account at [Vercel.com](https://vercel.com/) and log in.\n2. Click **Add New...** -> **Project**.\n3. Connect your GitHub account and select the repository you just exported.\n4. Vercel will automatically detect that it\'s a **Vite** project. Leave the Build Command (`npm run build`) and Output Directory (`dist`) as they are.\n\n### 3. Add Environment Variables (Crucial Step)\nBefore clicking \"Deploy\", expand the **Environment Variables** section and add your Supabase credentials so Vercel can connect to it:\n\n*   **Name:** `VITE_SUPABASE_URL`\n    **Value:** `https://bjqhwgskffdccrmveuxg.supabase.co`\n*   **Name:** `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`\n    **Value:** *(Paste that long key you shared with me earlier)*\n\n### 4. Deploy!\nClick the **Deploy** button. Vercel will build your app and give you a live URL (e.g., `https://hafra-dz-mvp.vercel.app`).\n\n### 5. Post-Deployment (Fixing Google Login for Vercel)\nBecause your domain will change from the AI Studio link to a Vercel link, you **must** tell Supabase where to redirect users after they log in with Google:\n\n1. Go to your **Supabase Dashboard**.\n2. Go to **Authentication** > **URL Configuration**.\n3. **Site URL:** Change this to your new Vercel URL (e.g., `https://hafra-dz-mvp.vercel.app`).\n4. **Redirect URLs:** Add your Vercel URL to the list of allowed callback URLs.\n\n*(Note: You do **not** need to change anything in the Google Cloud Console anymore! Google talks safely to Supabase, and Supabase talks to your Vercel app. You just need to update Supabase\'s Site URL).*\n\nThat\'s it! You will have a clean, production-ready MVP URL to share with your investors. Let me know if you run into any issues during the process!"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 333031150
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
