    thinking: "**Considering Alternatives**\n\nI\'m exploring options beyond Supabase for handling submissions. EmailJS or Web3Forms look promising as replacements, but a crucial hurdle emerges: rendering the map of other reports. Currently, the `reports` variable, populated from Supabase, fuels this map. Eliminating Supabase leaves a gap. I need to figure out where the map data will be served from.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Simplification**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a Minimal Viable Product approach. The user wants photo and info storage in Google Sheets/Excel or via email. The map of existing reports becomes less critical for this MVP, so I\'m shifting to how to get the data where they need it. It seems they want photo storage independent of the data, so Supabase for the JSON data is still in play, but storing the actual images is a new requirement. Email reports are the simplest, though static reports are another alternative.\n\n\n**Refining Data Collection**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a pure data collection tool, leveraging Vercel for hosting and emphasizing accurate GPS data. The key is data/photo storage, and the user\'s explicit preference for email or Google Sheets steers me towards a clean Web3Forms integration. Forget Firebase, the focus is simplicity: a Web3Forms script handles email submissions, and ImgBB manages image storage, directly addressing the core data needs.\n\n\n"
