  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Application Logic**\n\nI\'m removing the Supabase import from `src/app.js` and overriding the authentication logic. I\'ll read auth state directly from localStorage instead of relying on Supabase\'s `onAuthStateChange`. A `IS_CONFIGURED` variable is set to false.\n\n\n**Implementing Authentication Updates**\n\nI\'ve directly integrated localStorage to manage the user\'s email for authentication, removing Supabase dependencies. A `toggleAuth` function now handles login/logout, which toggles the email state in local storage and the UI accordingly. I\'m storing the user\'s email in `hafra_email`, and displaying a \"D\303\251connexion\" or \"Connexion MVP\" button.\n\n\n**Overriding MVP Functionality**\n\nI\'ve now overridden the `loadReports` and `subscribeRealtime` functions, implementing basic local storage management for MVP functionality. The upvote method also relies on local storage now. I\'m focusing on getting these core functions working with the minimal viable product.\n\n\n**Adding MVP Submission Function**\n\nI\'m adding the `submitReport` function now, along with checks for an internet connection and the `WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY`. I\'m setting a disabled state and showing a spinner while the report is sent. I plan to read photo data using FileReader to store a base64 version locally, for potential offline display. The function will be implemented with MVP functionality in mind.\n\n\n**Generating Report Payload**\n\nI\'m now generating the report payload. I\'m taking the photo file and converting it to a base64 string using a FileReader, handling null cases appropriately. I\'m also sanitizing the comment input, and constructing the payload object with a UUID, location data, score, category, comment, base64 photo data, user email (or \"Anonyme\"), Wilaya, vote count, status, and the current timestamp. The access key will be read from local storage, or retrieved via a prompt.\n\n\n**Finalizing Form Submission**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `web3forms` submission. I\'ve built the `formData` object, appending the access key, subject, message, category, Wilaya, position (Google Maps link), and gravity (star rating). I\'m also appending the photo file directly as an attachment. Error handling will be included. A success state will be displayed after submission.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 21
      nanos: 544236578
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
