  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I\'ve fixed the issue so `L.heatLayer` is correctly registered to the Leaflet object at runtime! \n\nThe problem was that module imports are hoisted and executed before the top-level assignments like `window.L = L`. Because `leaflet.heat` expects `L` to exist on the `window` object when it first parses, it couldn\'t find it. I\'ve reordered the imports dynamically (`await import(...)`) right after `window.L = L;` to ensure they\'re evaluated in the correct sequence!\n\nThe application has been successfully rebuilt without any errors and functions correctly again. Let me know if everything else is looking good to launch the MVP!"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
